c5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":9,"created_at":"2026-02-11T08:21:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T09:04:06Z","closed_at":"2026-02-16T07:01:21Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested & reproducible in 4.6-stable\n\n### System information\n\nUbuntu 24.04\n\n### Issue description\n\nIt seems `ViewportTexture` tries to resolve its `Viewport` `NodePath` relative to the scene that uses the texture, not the scene that \"contains\" the texture.\n\nThis yields the following error:\n```\nERROR: Path to node is invalid: 'Outer'.\n    at: _setup_local_to_scene (scene/main/viewport.cpp:199)\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create `root.tscn` with the following contents:\n1.1. `Control`\n1.1.1. `SubViewport`\n1.1.2. Instance of `scene.tscn`, texture set to `ViewportTexture` referencing the `SubViewport`\n2. Create `scene.tscn` with the following contents:\n2.1. `Sprite2D`\n\nClose and re-open the scene, and observe the printed error\n\nAlternatively: Open the MRP, observe the error upon opening `root.tscn`\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.tar.gz](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25228852/mrp.tar.gz)\n\n\n**EDIT:** This seems to happen even with Editable Children turned off on node 1.1.2.","closed_by":{"login":"gg-yb","id":76439353,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDM5MzUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76439353?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gg-yb","html_url":"https://github.com/gg-yb","followers_url":"https